<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salagama</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chalia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Salagama are a Sinhalese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">caste</a> of the south-western coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, traditionally associated with weaving and later with peeling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cinnamon">cinnamon</a>. Under the Portuguese and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, who drew great revenue from the island's cinnamon, they were required to collect and peel the bark as a service obligation. Many later prospered in trade, the professions and public life.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salagama.jpg" alt="Salagama" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sarathsilva · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:13th_Century_Salagama_Brahakmana_Flag.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
